# Quality Gates

- Keep lint, typecheck, unit tests, integration tests, and production build green.
- Add focused tests for every new behavior and regression fix.
- Add Playwright coverage for navigation, primary page flows, forms, keyboard use, and responsive layouts.
- Check 375, 480, 768, 1024, 1200, and 1440 pixel viewports for overflow and overlap.
- Test keyboard navigation, focus order, focus return, reduced motion, labels, errors, and media controls.
- Prevent horizontal scrolling unless explicitly specified for a controlled component.
- Target Lighthouse scores of at least 90 for Performance, Accessibility, Best Practices, and SEO on key pages.
- Target LCP at most 2.5 seconds, INP at most 200 milliseconds, and CLS at most 0.1 at p75.
- Review browser console errors, failed requests, hydration warnings, missing images, and broken links.
- Do not weaken checks, delete tests, or suppress errors merely to make a gate pass.
